e changed and judged by its own act still mints when a later act copies the same registry. That's deliberate: the lane pins it as minting, and the test's docstring gives the reason. On a squashed landing the ledger can't tell a routed change the row's own act judged from one a later copy absorbed after the act. Settling both would let an unjudged change vanish; minting both costs one redundant row. The rule takes the review-ward side, which is right.\n- **The proposed remedy is rejected for the same reason as in 013.** Proof bound to the row's own act can't be recovered on a squash without changing the ledger format.\n- **What's wrong is two promises the rule doesn't keep.**\n  - **Done-when item 1:** it says such a row \"yields no amendment row\", with no limit.\n  - **The landing recipe:** it says every row the sweep mints \"is real work and stays open\", which would have a coordinator keep a redundant row open and spend an adjudication on it.\n\n  Because this is a gap in the work item's own completion criteria, it can't be a successor row.\n- **The fix:**\n  - **Done-when item 1:** state its scope under a later copy in the spec's Trust section, next to item 5's.\n  - **LLR-364:** name this cost beside the rule's one limit.\n  - **The recipe:** narrow its sweep claim in both copies, telling the coordinator to check the row's own re-attesting act and close the row citing it when that act covered exactly those cells.\n\nThe verdict discloses that I ruled sitting 013 on this same rule and approved LLR-364 and TC-403 with it at sitting 014.\n\nThe commit hooks passed, but again reported that the `format` check didn't run (ruff isn't installed). I committed only the verdict, so `018-ADJUDICATE-e5811b9.md.requested` is still untracked.","ttft_ms":35803,"type":"result","duration_ms":179274,"uuid":"f103f8c4-5bd2-4621-8b05-4ef2fa6fd5b4","ttft_stream_ms":14853,"time_to_request_ms":163,"first_content_frame_ms":14853,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}]
